  "notes": [
    "Players and {name} take the honorific plural verb (చేరారు, గెలిచారు), which is gender-neutral; singular masculine/feminine verbs are never used for them. The fixed characters Akane, Yoru (she) and Gorō, the Shadow Captain (he) keep their genders.",
    "No case suffix or postposition is attached directly to a placeholder or #: a colon, a separate word (వరకు, తర్వాత, క్రితం, గారికి) or a noun after the placeholder carries the grammar.",
    "Plurals: one (1 only) and other (including 0), as Intl.PluralRules(\"te\") gives.",
    "Generated names use the default order (first part, space, second part): Telugu puts the modifier before the noun (ఉరుము + శిఖరం = ఉరుము శిఖరం). No generatedNames setting is needed.",
    "Japanese person names are transliterated into Telugu script (కైతో, తకేదా); Sensei Hoshi is గురువు హోషి.",
    "The Japanese statutory pages are translated in full into Telugu, as in the Hindi and Vietnamese catalogs; links to them from the support page keep the Japanese titles.",
    "ui.s_have_bced00a61e (\"s have\") is a plural fragment appended to \"Your purchase{arg1} been delivered\"; it is (లు), the usual Telugu way to mark an optional plural."
  ]
